"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[4047],{4047:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/phantom-lady.png\\"\\n          title=\\"Phantom Lady\\"\\n          author=\\"William Irish\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Chang\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2008-07-25\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9788974531577\\"\\n          rating=4.5\\n          tags=\\"mystery\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nOne of the books counted as the <mark>world\'s top three mystery novels</mark>.  \\nThe protagonist, who wandered the streets alone after a quarrel with his wife, happens to meet a woman wearing an ```orange``` hat, has dinner, and goes to the theater.  \\nThe protagonist returns home after parting with the woman, only to find his wife found as a corpse in the bedroom, and of course, the protagonist is designated as the first suspect.  \\nEven more, the dead wife was in a state of being strangled with the protagonist\'s tie.  \\n<br>\\nThe protagonist searches for the woman to prove his alibi, but knows nothing about her.  \\nEven the restaurant, the theater, and the taxi driver all say they did not see her.  \\n<br>\\nThis development causes an illusion for the readers as if the protagonist is the culprit.  \\n<br>\\nThis book is a classic mystery novel.  \\nOne shouldn\'t say, \\"Why is this one of the world\'s top three mystery novels?\\" after having already read many latest mystery novels.  \\nIt must have been an incredibly sensational work at that time.  \\n"}')}}]);